<title>FRANCE: Massonaud upgrades Bouygues Offshore.</title>
<headline>Massonaud upgrades Bouygues Offshore.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Broker Massonaud-Fonteny-Kervern upgraded its recommendation on Bouygues Offshore to buy from hold, market sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The broker considers that the company, a subsidiary of construction company Bouygues, has an active strategy and revised upward its 1997 profit forecast to 240 million francs from 167 million.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore was down 2.2 percent at 147 francs at 1157 GMT on volume of 7,170 shares. The market was up 1.2 percent. The stock had risen sharply after the firm reported 1996 results on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bouygues Offshore reported 1996 net attributable profit of 241 million francs, up from 170.7 million a year ago. It is aiming for 1997 sales of 3.9 billion,</p>
